1
00:00:15,660 --> 00:00:18,700
Up next, biological incidents.

2
00:00:18,700 --> 00:00:23,660
When you're dealing with pathogens or biological toxins, things get serious in a hurry.

3
00:00:23,660 --> 00:00:26,540
If there's an exposure, you don't have the luxury of taking your time.

4
00:00:26,540 --> 00:00:28,180
You need to act fast.

5
00:00:28,180 --> 00:00:30,220
So let's say there's a spill.

6
00:00:30,220 --> 00:00:32,260
Your first move has to be containment.

7
00:00:32,260 --> 00:00:36,220
That means laying down biohazard tape, getting anyone who doesn't need to be there out

8
00:00:36,220 --> 00:00:40,580
of the area, and if it's airborne, using biological safety cabinets.

9
00:00:40,580 --> 00:00:41,580
The goal is simple.

10
00:00:41,780 --> 00:00:45,460
To keep the danger contained so it doesn't spread and create an even bigger p-

11
00:00:46,460 --> 00:00:47,860
It's time to clean up.

12
00:00:47,860 --> 00:00:49,980
This is where you don't want to cut corners.

13
00:00:49,980 --> 00:00:53,940
Use the right disinfectants to make sure whatever you're dealing with is gone for good.

14
00:00:53,940 --> 00:00:58,180
If any equipment has to be contained, get it autoclaved so it's fully sterile.

15
00:00:58,180 --> 00:00:59,540
No half measures here.

16
00:00:59,540 --> 00:01:04,820
Now, if someone's exposed, say a needle stick happens with a potentially infected blood,

17
00:01:04,820 --> 00:01:06,900
immediate action is crucial.

18
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:11,300
You've got to wash the area with soap and water right away, no waiting around.

19
00:01:11,300 --> 00:01:14,140
After that, follow up with medical attention.

20
00:01:14,140 --> 00:01:17,460
Document what happened, and make sure you're getting the right treatment.

21
00:01:17,460 --> 00:01:22,140
If post-exposure prophylaxis, PP, is necessary, don't hesitate.

22
00:01:22,140 --> 00:01:23,140
Get it done.

23
00:01:23,140 --> 00:01:27,260
The CDC and OSHA have set the rules for handling biological hazards, and they're not just

24
00:01:27,260 --> 00:01:29,220
suggestions, they're essential.

25
00:01:29,220 --> 00:01:33,140
The Bloodborne Pathogen Standard makes sure you're following the right steps, from containment

26
00:01:33,140 --> 00:01:34,140
to disposal.

27
00:01:34,140 --> 00:01:38,760
So make sure you're disposing of contaminated materials properly, like using sharps containers

28
00:01:38,760 --> 00:01:39,760
for needles.

29
00:01:39,760 --> 00:01:44,080
It's all about sticking to the guidelines and keeping everyone safe.
